      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Over the last 4 years since installing the system we have not had any issues with our solar system. Our power bills are either in-credit month to month or are very small, the absolute most I have had to pay for a power bill in a month within the last 4 years was $250, which was during the winter months. The rest of the year we're either in credit or the bills are at most $100/month. We're able to run our AC all day every day, we're able to run the pool pump during the day, aside from shifting some of our energy usage to during the day when the FiT is lowest we have not had to change our energy habits much.Peter from Coastal Solar Solutions was very helpful in easing any concerns with getting a solar system, the installers on the day were very polite, they cleaned as they went and had the system installed and online by the end of the day. Once the system was installed they helped get the inverters online and we were off to the races.Our usage before the system was around 60KwH/day that has not changed since then but our 13.2kw system has offset 90% of that usage off of our bill. We are generating on avg. 50-60kwh/day from our system and most of that we use, our usage is now approx. 15kwh/day. After have a look at the inverters on the iSolarCloud site, the total yield for the last 4 years is 63 MWh. I can wholeheartedly endorse Steve Torpy and Coastal Solar Solutions for anyone looking to get a solar system installed.",
